From: Chromium-HaikuOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] build: Haiku toolchain fixes and compatibility headers

Applies after the FreeBSD 156.0.8078.79 patches, tools/haikuify.py and
patches 0001, 0002, 0004 and 0005. These are the build-system changes
found while bringing the first full `chrome` build up on Haiku (R1/beta6
development, x86_64, Clang 23), reduced for Renga (the Haiku fork,
Techniix/haiku ce/main), which provides the Linux interfaces that stock
Haiku needed stubs or helpers for.

build/config/haiku/BUILD.gn
  - defines: _LIBCPP_PROVIDES_DEFAULT_RUNE_TABLE (libc++ has no Haiku
    ctype table), CLOCK_BOOTTIME and CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW as
    CLOCK_MONOTONIC (Haiku has neither; it does not suspend, so the
    monotonic clock is boot time), IFF_RUNNING=IFF_LINK (Haiku's name for
    "carrier present"), RTLD_NODELETE=0 (not supported by the runtime
    loader).
  - compat/ is searched with -idirafter, so the stub headers only fill in
    what Haiku lacks and never shadow a real system header.
  - compat/haiku_cxx_prelude.h is force-included into C++ files: Haiku's
    <ctype.h> defines isalpha() and friends as macros, which breaks
    libc++'s <cctype> (`using ::isalpha;`).
  - runtime_library: the Haiku Clang driver puts GCC's header directory
    (/boot/system/develop/headers/gcc/include) ahead of Clang's builtin
    headers, and GCC's <stdatomic.h> and intrinsics headers do not compile
    with Clang. Clang's resource directory is put first; the path is
    filled in by scripts/prepare-tree.sh (@CLANG_RESOURCE_DIR@).
    clang_first/stdatomic.h is Clang's own header with the
    __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>) branch disabled, so C11 atomics do
    not fall through to GCC's version.
  - libgnu is linked into every target. Renga's Linux interfaces (epoll,
    eventfd, inotify, memfd_create, backtrace, getauxval, getdents64, ...)
    are there, with their headers in the gnu header directory, which the
    Haiku Clang driver already searches (_GNU_SOURCE is defined).
    getpeereid() is in libbsd, which patch 0001 already links.
  - compat/lib is added to the library search path. It holds empty
    libdl/librt/libpthread archives (these live in libroot on Haiku, but
    Linux build files name them) and libm.a, which is a linker script:
    libm is part of libroot too, and the script pulls in libhaikucompat.a
    (the Media Kit audio shim of patch 0011, built by scripts/build.sh)
    with libmedia and libbe. Renga has sched_getaffinity() and
    pthread_getaffinity_np() in libroot, so the stock-Haiku script's
    AS_NEEDED(-lgnu) is gone.

build/config/haiku/compat/*: header stubs for Linux-only includes that
are reached unconditionally: <endian.h> and <sys/endian.h> (byte-order
macros on compiler builtins), <sys/syscall.h>,
<sys/sysmacros.h> (DRM code only), <net/if_arp.h> (ARPHRD_* mapped to IFT_ETHER),
<linux/input.h> with linux/input-event-codes.h (the Linux UAPI header,
GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note, used only for key code numbers by the
Wayland keyboard code) and linux/haiku_ioc.h (_IO/_IOR/_IOW encodings
for code that only builds ioctl numbers).

build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni: clang_toolchain() used plain
cc/c++/ar/nm/readelf, which are GCC and GNU binutils on Haiku; use
clang, clang++ and the llvm-* tools.

build/config/ui.gni: no ATK/AT-SPI on Haiku.

BUILD.gn: //build/modules (Clang modules over /usr/include) is left out
of gn_all; Haiku has no /usr/include.

buildtools/third_party/libc++abi: no futex on Haiku (Renga roadmap
F-49), use the generic mutex/condition variable implementation. Renga's
libroot provides __cxa_thread_atexit_impl() (thread_local destructors,
including the main thread's at exit()), so cxa_thread_atexit.cpp is built
with HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL and its __cxa_thread_atexit() entry
point is enabled for __HAIKU__ (third_party/libc++abi). This replaces the
stock-Haiku compat/lib/haiku_cxa_thread_atexit.c helper.

third_party/typescript/tsgo.gni, devtools typescript_vars.gni: treat a
Haiku host like Linux. On Haiku the "tsgo" binary is a wrapper around the
JavaScript TypeScript compiler written by prepare-tree.sh.

mojo/public/tools/bindings/mojom.gni: haikuify turned the FreeBSD/OpenBSD
"is_bsd" mojom feature string into the GN expression "(is_bsd ||
is_haiku)", which mojom does not understand. Restore "is_bsd" and add an
"is_haiku" feature for Haiku.

third_party/nasm/BUILD.gn: read Haiku's <string.h> to detect mempcpy.

third_party/fontconfig/BUILD.gn: libuuid is not needed on Haiku (and its
devel package pulled in a system-header update mid-build).
---
diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index 3f53c0f..3940386 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ group("gn_all") {
     deps = [
       "//base:base_perftests",
       "//base:base_unittests",
-      "//build/modules",
+      # "//build/modules",  # Haiku: no /usr/include
       "//codelabs",
       "//components:components_unittests",
       "//components/gwp_asan:gwp_asan_unittests",
diff --git a/build/config/haiku/BUILD.gn b/build/config/haiku/BUILD.gn
index 5cb5066..430b475 100644
--- a/build/config/haiku/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/haiku/BUILD.gn
@@ -13,17 +13,57 @@ config("compiler") {
     # pipe2) behind these feature macros.
     "_DEFAULT_SOURCE",
     "_GNU_SOURCE",
+
+    # libc++ has no Haiku ctype/rune table; use its built-in classic table.
+    "_LIBCPP_PROVIDES_DEFAULT_RUNE_TABLE",
+
+    # No suspend on Haiku: monotonic == boot time.
+    "CLOCK_BOOTTIME=CLOCK_MONOTONIC",
+    "CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW=CLOCK_MONOTONIC",
+
+    # Haiku spells "interface has carrier" IFF_LINK.
+    "IFF_RUNNING=IFF_LINK",
+
+    # No RTLD_NODELETE in Haiku's runtime loader.
+    "RTLD_NODELETE=0",
   ]
   cflags = [
     # The Linux configs pass a few flags (e.g. -pthread, -fstack-clash-protection)
     # that the Haiku Clang driver accepts but ignores; don't let the resulting
     # warnings break -Werror builds.
     "-Wno-unused-command-line-argument",
+
+    # Stubs for Linux-only <sys/...> headers (build/config/haiku/compat).
+    "-idirafter",
+    rebase_path("compat", root_build_dir),
+  ]
+  cflags_cc = [
+    "-include",
+    rebase_path("compat/haiku_cxx_prelude.h", root_build_dir),
   ]
 }
 
 # Applied to every target through //build/config/compiler:runtime_library.
 config("runtime_library") {
+  # The Haiku Clang driver searches /boot/system/develop/headers/gcc/include
+  # (GCC's intrinsics and <stdatomic.h>) ahead of Clang's own builtin headers,
+  # which Clang can't compile. Put Clang's first. This config is applied after
+  # libc++'s, so libc++'s -isystem dirs still come before it.
+  clang_builtin_headers = "@CLANG_RESOURCE_DIR@/include"  # set by prepare-tree.sh
+  clang_first = rebase_path("clang_first", root_build_dir)
+  cflags_c = [ "-isystem", clang_first, "-isystem", clang_builtin_headers ]
+  cflags_cc = [ "-isystem", clang_first, "-isystem", clang_builtin_headers ]
+  cflags_objc = cflags_c
+  cflags_objcc = cflags_cc
+  ldflags = [ "-L" + rebase_path("compat/lib", root_build_dir) ]
+
+  # Renga: the Linux interfaces Chromium uses (epoll, eventfd, inotify,
+  # memfd_create, backtrace, getdents64, ...) live in libgnu, with their
+  # headers in the gnu header directory that the Haiku Clang driver already
+  # searches. Link it everywhere, as Linux links these from libc.
+  # (libbsd, with getpeereid(), is in //build/config:default_libs.)
+  libs = [ "gnu" ]
+
   # libroot (libc, libm, pthreads, libdl) is linked implicitly by the Haiku
   # Clang driver. libnetwork is added in //build/config:default_libs.
 }
diff --git a/build/config/haiku/clang_first/stdatomic.h b/build/config/haiku/clang_first/stdatomic.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0724478
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/config/haiku/clang_first/stdatomic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,205 @@
+// Copied from /boot/system/lib/clang/23/include/stdatomic.h by haiku-fixes-pass4.sh
+/*===---- stdatomic.h - Standard header for atomic types and operations -----===
+ *
+ * Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
+ * See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+ *
+ *===-----------------------------------------------------------------------===
+ */
+
+#ifndef __CLANG_STDATOMIC_H
+#define __CLANG_STDATOMIC_H
+
+/* If we're hosted, fall back to the system's stdatomic.h. FreeBSD, for
+ * example, already has a Clang-compatible stdatomic.h header.
+ *
+ * Exclude the MSVC path as well as the MSVC header as of the 14.31.30818
+ * explicitly disallows `stdatomic.h` in the C mode via an `#error`.  Fallback
+ * to the clang resource header until that is fully supported.  The
+ * `stdatomic.h` header requires C++23 or newer.
+ */
+#if __STDC_HOSTED__ &&                                                         \
+    0 /* Haiku: never use GCC's stdatomic.h */ &&                                       \
+    (!defined(_MSC_VER) || (defined(__cplusplus) && __cplusplus >= 202002L))
+# include_next <stdatomic.h>
+#else
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+/* 7.17.1 Introduction */
+
+#define ATOMIC_BOOL_LOCK_FREE       __CLANG_ATOMIC_BOOL_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_CHAR_LOCK_FREE       __CLANG_ATOMIC_CHAR_LOCK_FREE
+#if defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L
+#define ATOMIC_CHAR8_T_LOCK_FREE    __CLANG_ATOMIC_CHAR8_T_LOCK_FREE
+#endif
+#define ATOMIC_CHAR16_T_LOCK_FREE   __CLANG_ATOMIC_CHAR16_T_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_CHAR32_T_LOCK_FREE   __CLANG_ATOMIC_CHAR32_T_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_WCHAR_T_LOCK_FREE    __CLANG_ATOMIC_WCHAR_T_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_SHORT_LOCK_FREE      __CLANG_ATOMIC_SHORT_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_INT_LOCK_FREE        __CLANG_ATOMIC_INT_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_LONG_LOCK_FREE       __CLANG_ATOMIC_LONG_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_LLONG_LOCK_FREE      __CLANG_ATOMIC_LLONG_LOCK_FREE
+#define ATOMIC_POINTER_LOCK_FREE    __CLANG_ATOMIC_POINTER_LOCK_FREE
+
+/* 7.17.2 Initialization */
+#if (defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ < 202311L) ||               \
+    defined(__cplusplus)
+/* ATOMIC_VAR_INIT was removed in C23, but still remains in C++23. */
+#define ATOMIC_VAR_INIT(value) (value)
+#endif
+
+#if ((defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 201710L &&              \
+      __STDC_VERSION__ < 202311L) ||                                           \
+     (defined(__cplusplus) && __cplusplus >= 202002L)) &&                      \
+    !defined(_CLANG_DISABLE_CRT_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS)
+/* ATOMIC_VAR_INIT was deprecated in C17 and C++20. */
+#pragma clang deprecated(ATOMIC_VAR_INIT)
+#endif
+#define atomic_init __c11_atomic_init
+
+/* 7.17.3 Order and consistency */
+
+typedef enum memory_order {
+  memory_order_relaxed = __ATOMIC_RELAXED,
+  memory_order_consume = __ATOMIC_CONSUME,
+  memory_order_acquire = __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE,
+  memory_order_release = __ATOMIC_RELEASE,
+  memory_order_acq_rel = __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL,
+  memory_order_seq_cst = __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST
+} memory_order;
+
+#define kill_dependency(y) (y)
+
+/* 7.17.4 Fences */
+
+/* These should be provided by the libc implementation. */
+void atomic_thread_fence(memory_order);
+void atomic_signal_fence(memory_order);
+
+#define atomic_thread_fence(order) __c11_atomic_thread_fence(order)
+#define atomic_signal_fence(order) __c11_atomic_signal_fence(order)
+
+/* 7.17.5 Lock-free property */
+
+#define atomic_is_lock_free(obj) __c11_atomic_is_lock_free(sizeof(*(obj)))
+
+/* 7.17.6 Atomic integer types */
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+typedef _Atomic(bool)               atomic_bool;
+#else
+typedef _Atomic(_Bool)              atomic_bool;
+#endif
+typedef _Atomic(char)               atomic_char;
+typedef _Atomic(signed char)        atomic_schar;
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned char)      atomic_uchar;
+typedef _Atomic(short)              atomic_short;
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned short)     atomic_ushort;
+typedef _Atomic(int)                atomic_int;
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned int)       atomic_uint;
+typedef _Atomic(long)               atomic_long;
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned long)      atomic_ulong;
+typedef _Atomic(long long)          atomic_llong;
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned long long) atomic_ullong;
+#if defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L
+typedef _Atomic(unsigned char)      atomic_char8_t;
+#endif
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least16_t)     atomic_char16_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least32_t)     atomic_char32_t;
+typedef _Atomic(wchar_t)            atomic_wchar_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_least8_t)       atomic_int_least8_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least8_t)      atomic_uint_least8_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_least16_t)      atomic_int_least16_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least16_t)     atomic_uint_least16_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_least32_t)      atomic_int_least32_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least32_t)     atomic_uint_least32_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_least64_t)      atomic_int_least64_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_least64_t)     atomic_uint_least64_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_fast8_t)        atomic_int_fast8_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_fast8_t)       atomic_uint_fast8_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_fast16_t)       atomic_int_fast16_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_fast16_t)      atomic_uint_fast16_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_fast32_t)       atomic_int_fast32_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_fast32_t)      atomic_uint_fast32_t;
+typedef _Atomic(int_fast64_t)       atomic_int_fast64_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uint_fast64_t)      atomic_uint_fast64_t;
+typedef _Atomic(intptr_t)           atomic_intptr_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uintptr_t)          atomic_uintptr_t;
+typedef _Atomic(size_t)             atomic_size_t;
+typedef _Atomic(ptrdiff_t)          atomic_ptrdiff_t;
+typedef _Atomic(intmax_t)           atomic_intmax_t;
+typedef _Atomic(uintmax_t)          atomic_uintmax_t;
+
+/* 7.17.7 Operations on atomic types */
+
+#define atomic_store(object, desired) __c11_atomic_store(object, desired, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_store_explicit __c11_atomic_store
+
+#define atomic_load(object) __c11_atomic_load(object, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_load_explicit __c11_atomic_load
+
+#define atomic_exchange(object, desired) __c11_atomic_exchange(object, desired, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_exchange_explicit __c11_atomic_exchange
+
+#define atomic_compare_exchange_strong(object, expected, desired) __c11_atomic_compare_exchange_strong(object, expected, desired, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_compare_exchange_strong_explicit __c11_atomic_compare_exchange_strong
+
+#define atomic_compare_exchange_weak(object, expected, desired) __c11_atomic_compare_exchange_weak(object, expected, desired, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_compare_exchange_weak_explicit __c11_atomic_compare_exchange_weak
+
+#define atomic_fetch_add(object, operand) __c11_atomic_fetch_add(object, operand, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_fetch_add_explicit __c11_atomic_fetch_add
+
+#define atomic_fetch_sub(object, operand) __c11_atomic_fetch_sub(object, operand, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_fetch_sub_explicit __c11_atomic_fetch_sub
+
+#define atomic_fetch_or(object, operand) __c11_atomic_fetch_or(object, operand, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_fetch_or_explicit __c11_atomic_fetch_or
+
+#define atomic_fetch_xor(object, operand) __c11_atomic_fetch_xor(object, operand, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_fetch_xor_explicit __c11_atomic_fetch_xor
+
+#define atomic_fetch_and(object, operand) __c11_atomic_fetch_and(object, operand, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_fetch_and_explicit __c11_atomic_fetch_and
+
+/* 7.17.8 Atomic flag type and operations */
+
+typedef struct atomic_flag { atomic_bool _Value; } atomic_flag;
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+#define ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT {false}
+#else
+#define ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT { 0 }
+#endif
+
+/* These should be provided by the libc implementation. */
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+bool atomic_flag_test_and_set(volatile atomic_flag *);
+bool atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(volatile atomic_flag *, memory_order);
+#else
+_Bool atomic_flag_test_and_set(volatile atomic_flag *);
+_Bool atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(volatile atomic_flag *, memory_order);
+#endif
+void atomic_flag_clear(volatile atomic_flag *);
+void atomic_flag_clear_explicit(volatile atomic_flag *, memory_order);
+
+#define atomic_flag_test_and_set(object) __c11_atomic_exchange(&(object)->_Value, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(object, order) __c11_atomic_exchange(&(object)->_Value, 1, order)
+
+#define atomic_flag_clear(object) __c11_atomic_store(&(object)->_Value, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST)
+#define atomic_flag_clear_explicit(object, order) __c11_atomic_store(&(object)->_Value, 0, order)
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif /* __STDC_HOSTED__ */
+#endif /* __CLANG_STDATOMIC_H */
+
diff --git a/build/config/haiku/compat/endian.h b/build/config/haiku/compat/endian.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..810c215
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/config/haiku/compat/endian.h
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+// Haiku compat <endian.h> (glibc/BSD style), built on compiler builtins.
+#ifndef HAIKU_COMPAT_ENDIAN_H
+#define HAIKU_COMPAT_ENDIAN_H
+#include <stdint.h>
+#ifndef __LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#define __LITTLE_ENDIAN __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__
+#define __BIG_ENDIAN __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+#define __PDP_ENDIAN __ORDER_PDP_ENDIAN__
+#define __BYTE_ORDER __BYTE_ORDER__
+#endif
+#ifndef LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#define LITTLE_ENDIAN __LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#define BIG_ENDIAN __BIG_ENDIAN
+#define PDP_ENDIAN __PDP_ENDIAN
+#endif
+#ifndef BYTE_ORDER
+#define BYTE_ORDER __BYTE_ORDER
+#endif
+#if __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__
+#define HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(b, x) ((uint##b##_t)(x))
+#define HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(b, x) ((uint##b##_t)__builtin_bswap##b(x))
+#else
+#define HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(b, x) ((uint##b##_t)__builtin_bswap##b(x))
+#define HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(b, x) ((uint##b##_t)(x))
+#endif
+#ifndef htole16
+#define htole16(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(16, x)
+#define htole32(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(32, x)
+#define htole64(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(64, x)
+#define le16toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(16, x)
+#define le32toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(32, x)
+#define le64toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_LE(64, x)
+#endif
+#ifndef htobe16
+#define htobe16(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(16, x)
+#define htobe32(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(32, x)
+#define htobe64(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(64, x)
+#define be16toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(16, x)
+#define be32toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(32, x)
+#define be64toh(x) HAIKU_COMPAT_BE(64, x)
+#endif
+#endif
